---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// A faithfully rendered coach exchange. Voice + rules per docs/COACH_PROMPT.md;
// the tool call, inline [note_id] citations, the [personal_finding] distinction,
// and "numbers only from tool results" are the coach loop from INTELLIGENCE.md §4.
---

<Section
  n="02"
  id="coach"
  tone="sunk"
  labelledby="coach-h"
  note="The coach reasons over 30–90 days of your data, not a snapshot — INTELLIGENCE.md §4."
>
  <p class="eyebrow rise">The coach, rendered</p>
  <h2 id="coach-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
    It calls a tool for the number, then tells you what it actually means.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    An uncited coach can say anything. Ours reads your data through tools, cites every claim to a
    research note or your own history, and hedges to match the evidence.<sup class="ref"
      ><a href="#ref-10" aria-label="reference 10">10</a></sup
    >
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a coach exchange about a weekly HRV dip"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        Transcript &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">grounded coach</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;Why is my HRV down this week?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <!-- the visible mechanism -->
    <div class="toolcall mt-6" role="group" aria-label="Tool call the coach made">
      <span class="toolcall-tag">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> tool call &middot; query_metric
      </span>
      <div>
        <span class="k">{'{'} metric:</span> <span class="v">"hrv_sleep_avg"</span><span class="k"
          >, window:</span
        > <span class="v">"7d"</span><span class="k">, stat:</span> <span class="v">"series"</span>
        <span class="k">{'}'}</span>
        <span class="ret"
          >&larr; returns: 7 nights &middot; avg <span class="v">39&nbsp;ms</span> &middot; your
          baseline <span class="v">46&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;6&nbsp;ms</span></span
        >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="turn turn-coach mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">Coach</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Your overnight HRV has run about <span class="mono">39&nbsp;ms</span> this week against your
          own <span class="mono">46&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;6</span> baseline &mdash; a real dip, not
          day-to-day noise <span class="cite">[hrv_recovery_marker]</span>. HRV is a recovery signal,
          but a noisy one night to night, so I&rsquo;m reading the week, not any single morning.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Before you call it lost fitness, look at your log: on the three nights you recorded a late
          drink, your HRV dropped the next morning
          <span class="cite cite-personal">[personal_finding: late_alcohol&rarr;hrv]</span> &mdash;
          that&rsquo;s <em>your</em> pattern, not a population average pinned onto you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Smallest lever this week: two alcohol-free nights, then we re-read the trend. I won&rsquo;t
          score seven days of a confounded signal as recovery loss.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        <span class="text-accent-soft">[note_id]</span> resolves to a real research note; the
        red-lead marks a citation, the gold a finding from
        <span class="text-gold">your own data</span> &mdash; never dressed as research.
      </p>
      <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Every number here came from the <span class="text-ink">query_metric</span> result above. The
        coach never guesses yours &mdash; if a tool didn&rsquo;t return it, it doesn&rsquo;t have it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </figure>
</Section>
